#: ../../source/undici_README.md:660
msgid "Expect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:662
msgid ""
"Undici does not support the `Expect` request header field. The request "
"body is  always immediately sent and the `100 Continue` response will be "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:666
msgid "Refs: https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7231#section-5.1.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:668
msgid "Pipelining"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:670
msgid ""
"Undici will only use pipelining if configured with a `pipelining` factor "
"greater than `1`. Also it is important to pass `blocking: false` to the "
"request options to properly pipeline requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:674
msgid ""
"Undici always assumes that connections are persistent and will "
"immediately pipeline requests, without checking whether the connection is"
" persistent. Hence, automatic fallback to HTTP/1.0 or HTTP/1.1 without "
"pipelining is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:679
msgid ""
"Undici will immediately pipeline when retrying requests after a failed "
"connection. However, Undici will not retry the first remaining requests "
"in the prior pipeline and instead error the corresponding "
"callback/promise/stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:683
msgid ""
"Undici will abort all running requests in the pipeline when any of them "
"are aborted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:686
msgid "Refs: https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2616#section-8.1.2.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:687
msgid "Refs: https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7230#section-6.3.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:689
msgid "Manual Redirect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:691
msgid ""
"Since it is not possible to manually follow an HTTP redirect on the "
"server-side, Undici returns the actual response instead of an "
"`opaqueredirect` filtered one when invoked with a `manual` redirect. This"
" aligns `fetch()` with the other implementations in Deno and Cloudflare "
"Workers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:696
msgid "Refs: https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#atomic-http-redirect-handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:698
msgid "Workarounds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:700
msgid "Network address family autoselection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:702
msgid ""
"If you experience problem when connecting to a remote server that is "
"resolved by your DNS servers to a IPv6 (AAAA record) first, there are "
"chances that your local router or ISP might have problem connecting to "
"IPv6 networks. In that case undici will throw an error with code "
"`UND_ERR_CONNECT_TIMEOUT`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/undici_README.md:706
msgid ""
"If the target server resolves to both a IPv6 and IPv4 (A records) address"
" and you are using a compatible Node version (18.3.0 and above), you can "
"fix the problem by providing the `autoSelectFamily` option (support by "
"both `undici.request` and `undici.Agent`) which will enable the family "
"autoselection algorithm when establishing the connection."
msgstr ""

